usage: flair combine [-h] (--manifest MANIFEST | --prefixes PREFIXES |
                     --isoform_beds ISOFORM_BEDS) -g GENOME [-f GTF]
                     [-o OUTPUT] [--end_window END_WINDOW]
                     [--frac_support FRAC_SUPPORT] [--remove_single_exon]
                     [--max_ends MAX_ENDS] [--min_reads MIN_READS]

Combine FLAIR transcriptomes into one. Each input is a flair BED, with the
read support columns flair transcriptome, flair fusion and flair isoalleles
write

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -f, --gtf GTF         an annotation GTF. With it, each combined isoform is
                        given its gene, reference transcript, CDS,
                        productivity and protein from this annotation, as
                        flair transcriptome gives them, whatever annotation
                        the samples were run with, so samples run with
                        different annotations or FLAIR versions can be
                        combined, and the proteins are written to
                        combined.aaseq.tsv. Fusion isoforms keep the samples'
                        genes. Without it, the samples' genes, CDS and
                        productivity are used, isoforms from different samples
                        with different genes are an error, and isoforms have
                        no protein ids
  -o, --output OUTPUT   prefix for output file (default: flair)
  --end_window END_WINDOW
                        window, in bases, for comparing ends of isoforms with
                        the same intron chain (default: 200)
  --frac_support FRAC_SUPPORT
                        minimum share of its gene's reads for an isoform, in
                        one sample, to be kept in the combined transcriptome;
                        taken from frac_support, column 17 of the input BEDs:
                        an isoform without it is an error (default: 0.05)
  --remove_single_exon  remove all single exon isoforms
  --max_ends MAX_ENDS   how the ends of a splice junction chain are combined:
                        - 1: the chain gives one isoform, containing the
                          isoforms of every group of similar ends and their
                          read support
                        - above 1: each group of similar ends gives an isoform
                          of its own, when the group passes --frac_support and
                          --min_reads on its own, so ends are more precise and
                          the support of a group that fails them is dropped.
                          Any value above 1 gives the same result
                        (default: 1)
  --min_reads MIN_READS
                        min reads from all samples to call isoform; taken from
                        read_support, column 16 of the input BEDs: an isoform
                        without it is an error (default: 3)

required named arguments:
  --manifest MANIFEST   file naming the flair isoform BEDs to combine, one
                        path a line, as in path/to/isoforms.bed. Blank lines
                        and lines starting with '#' are skipped; each BED once
  --prefixes PREFIXES   prefixes of the FLAIR transcriptomes to combine, each
                        naming PREFIX.isoforms.bed and including any
                        directories; give several comma separated, or repeat
                        the option, or both
  --isoform_beds ISOFORM_BEDS
                        paths of the flair isoform BEDs to combine; give
                        several comma separated, or repeat the option, or both
  -g, --genome GENOME   genome FASTA, read for the isoform sequences, the
                        protein predictions and the chromosome sizes of the
                        bigBed
